<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<section xml:id="sec_recursion_cosine">
        <title>Creating a Theoretical Model with the Cosine</title>
        <p>
                Use the data you recorded in <xref ref='tab_important_dates'/>
                to compute the appropriate parameters, <m>a_{2}</m>, <m>k_{2}</m>, <m>t_{2}</m>, and <m>m_{2}</m> to correctly fit your data with the function
                <md>h_{2}(t)=a_{2}\cos\left(k_{2}(t-t_{2})\right)+m_{2}</md>
                where <m>t</m> is time in days (measured from your reference time), and <m>h_{2}(t)</m> is hours of daylight.
        </p>
        <p>
                Note that some of these parameters may be the same as in your model using sine, but they will not all be the same!
        </p>
                <p>
                        We will now compare your sine and cosine models.
                        <ol>
                                <li>
                                        <p>
                                                What is the <em>period</em> of the cosine function in your theoretical cosine model? How does this compare to the period of the function you defined in <xref ref="sec_recursion_sine"/>?
                                        </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                        <p>
                                                What is the <em>amplitude</em> of the cosine function in your theoretical cosine model? How does this compare to the amplitude of the function you defined in <xref ref="sec_recursion_sine"/>?
                                        </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                        <p>
                                                What is the <em>midline</em> of the cosine function in your theoretical cosine model? How does this compare to the midline of the function you defined in <xref ref="sec_recursion_sine"/>?
                                        </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                        <p>
                                                What is the <em>horizontal shift</em> of the cosine function in your theoretical cosine model? How does this compare to the horizontal shift of the function you defined in <xref ref="sec_recursion_sine"/>?
                                        </p>
                                </li>
                        </ol>
                </p>
</section>
